flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box.guard has an empty command, which names no program to run.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box.masks has "rel", which is not a string matching the pattern /.*.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box.limits.CPUQuota is "0%", which is not a string matching the pattern [1-9][0-9]*%.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box.seccomp.allow has "Ptrace", which is not a string matching the pattern @?[a-z0-9_-]+.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box drives containers.box, and would bind /proc/1 into a session. That reaches flong's state, the user manager's bus or private socket, /proc, the cgroup filesystem or a path in flong.box.protect, any of which lets a session act as the caller outside it. The check here is lexical; the launcher's canonical one refuses the rest at launch.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box masks /srv/b/x/y (in the writable bind of /srv/b), two or more levels below the root of a writable bind. A session that can write the host directory can rename the masked file's parent and leave a decoy for the mask to cover, and the file shows through at the new name. Mask at most one level below the root of the writable bind named, or make that bind read-only.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box drives containers.box, whose allowedDevices has /srv/null r. A device is bound read-write, so the node must be under /dev/ and the modifier "rw" or "rwm" (m means nothing for a bound node).
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box drives containers.box, which binds /dev/snd. A plain bind is nodev, so the device would mount and then refuse every open. List it in allowedDevices instead, and drop the bind.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box drives containers.box as u (70000:100), outside the container's ids 0-65535.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box drives containers.box, and rel is not a clean absolute path: it is /, or has a trailing slash, an empty, . or .. component, or a component over 255 bytes. The launcher would refuse it at launch.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box drives containers.box, and mounts something at /srv/b twice: as two of a bind, a mask, a tmpfs, an overlay or a device. The launcher mounts one thing at each path.
flong check: @GOLDEN@/decl/every-refusal-at-once.zon: flong.box sets seccomp.tier = null and seccomp.allow, which change a tier's allow-list. With no tier there is no filter for them to act on. Set a tier, or drop them.
